## Key Observations

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Top-line growth:</strong> ABHI's <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">Total GWP of ₹1,041 cr</span> represents <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">▲35% YoY growth</span>, with Retail health GWP contributing ₹551 cr (~53% of the mix). SAHI market share rose to <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">▲12.5%</span> (+92 bps YoY).
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Profitability still negative but improving:</strong> ABHI reported a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">Pre-Tax Loss (PBT, IND AS) of ₹(51) crore</span> in Q1 FY25, narrower than the ₹(62) crore loss in Q1 FY24 — a directional improvement, though the standalone statutory PAT figure was not disclosed in the sources reviewed.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Combined ratio trending favorably:</strong> The reported Combined ratio <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">▼improved to 112%</span> from 118% in Q1 FY24 — a **6 percentage-point** improvement, consistent with the narrowing loss trend, though it remains above the 100% profitability breakeven threshold.
</div>

